/-!
# Proper integral toric towers after arbitrary base change

Source: ILO VIII 3.2.9, 3.2.17--3.2.18, 3.3.5--3.3.11; the integral-coefficient
formulation of O1 (blueprint: lem-per-integral-toric-tower-proper).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Monoscheme

/-- Integral saturated toric towers are proper, have the prescribed finite tensor
charts and monomial localizations, and are unchanged over the monomial-invertible locus.
Multiplicative notation presents the source's additive monoids without changing them.
Source: ILO VIII 3.2.9, 3.2.17--3.2.18, 3.3.5--3.3.11; O1 integral formulation
(blueprint: lem-per-integral-toric-tower-proper).

Proof (the eight DAG steps):
1. Induct on the tower. A coherent center on a fine affine monoid has finite
nonempty generators E. For a ∈ E the next chart is the saturation of the monoid
generated by Q and b/a. `lem-trf-fine-monoid-finite-saturation` preserves fineness,
group completion and compatibility with localization. This gives finite covers.
2. Inside Z[G], the ordinary blowup chart Z[Q][J/z^a] is exactly Z[Q[E/a]].
Translate exponents to check injectivity and compare the monomial bases; use
`prop-nagata-affine-blowup-chart-cover` and `def-nagata-blowup-chart-ring`.
3. `prop-nagata-affine-blowup-chart`, `def-nagata-affine-blowup-chart-map` and
`def-nagata-homogeneous-away-to-chart` identify its overlaps as D(z^(b/a)).
`lem-weil-pbc-proj-standard-open-inclusion` computes their intersections.
The same formulas commute with monoid localization. The ordinary blowup is
proper by `lemma-nagata-affine-blowup-proper`.
4. Saturation gives a finite map on each chart, by the finite-saturation lemma
and `lem-weil-pbc-spec-finite-ring-map-finite`. Its full inverse image of the
ordinary chart is the saturated chart: check this on every overlap. Hence it
is finite by `lem-weil-pbc-finite-local-on-target`.
5. Use `lem-weil-pbc-finite-proper`, `lem-weil-pbc-proper-composition` and
`lemma-nagata-projective-target-local` to glue properness of each integral step.
6. Pull back the chart cover using `lem-weil-pbc-open-fibre-product` and identify
the rings using `lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-affine-spectra`. Localization sends
(a ⊗ z^q)/(1 ⊗ z^t) to a ⊗ z^(q/t); its inverse sends this monomial back to the
fraction. `lem-weil-pbc-ring-localization-universal-property` checks both composites.
Finite monoid generation reduces any such localization to a principal open.
The overlap maps are the same monomial maps after tensoring.
7. Pullback pasting identifies each base-changed step with a base change of its
integral step. Apply `lem-weil-pbc-proper-base-change` and proper composition.
The length-zero case is the identity; the zero ring gives empty schemes.
8. Inverting P changes every Q to G. The map L ⊗ Z[Q] → L sends l ⊗ z^(p/p')
to l α(p)/α(p'). Integrality proves independence of this expression. Every
overlap becomes all of Spec L with identity transition, so the charts glue to
Spec L. Localization has exactly the stated denominators, even if L is zero.
-/
theorem integral_toric_tower_proper
    (P : Type u) [CommMonoid P] (hfs : IsFineSaturatedMonoid P)
    (htf : ∀ (g : Algebra.GrothendieckGroup P) (m : ℕ), 0 < m → g ^ m = 1 → g = 1)
    (n : ℕ) (T : Tower.{u} n) (e : (T.level 0).space ≅ affine P)
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (α : P →* A) :
    (∀ j : Fin n, IsProper (integralBaseMap A α (T.arrow j).map
      (T.integralSpaceToBase e j.castSucc))) ∧
    (∀ i : Fin (n + 1), IsProper
      (integralBaseProjection A α (T.integralSpaceToBase e i))) ∧
    (∀ i : Fin (n + 1), ∃ r : ℕ,
      ∃ C : Fin r → IntegralToricChart (T.integralSpaceToBase e i),
        (∀ x : (T.level i).space, ∃ j : Fin r, x ∈ (C j).chart.openSet) ∧
        (∀ j : Fin r, IsOpenImmersion ((C j).baseChangeι A α)) ∧
        (∀ x : integralBaseChange A α (T.integralSpaceToBase e i),
          ∃ j : Fin r, x ∈ Set.range ((C j).baseChangeι A α))) ∧
    (∀ (i : Fin (n + 1))
      (C D : IntegralToricChart (T.integralSpaceToBase e i))
      (ψ : D.monoid →* C.monoid)
      (f : affine C.monoid ⟶ affine D.monoid),
      IsAffineMap ψ f → C.chart.inclusion = f ≫ D.chart.inclusion →
      ∃ l : logIdealTensorRing A α (integralChartInclusion D.monoid D.containsBase) →+*
          logIdealTensorRing A α (integralChartInclusion C.monoid C.containsBase),
        (∀ a : A,
          l (logIdealTensorBase A α (integralChartInclusion D.monoid D.containsBase) a) =
            logIdealTensorBase A α (integralChartInclusion C.monoid C.containsBase) a) ∧
        (∀ q : D.monoid,
          l (logIdealTensorMonomial A α (integralChartInclusion D.monoid D.containsBase) q) =
            logIdealTensorMonomial A α (integralChartInclusion C.monoid C.containsBase)
              (ψ q)) ∧
        C.baseChangeι A α = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom l) ≫ D.baseChangeι A α) ∧
    (∀ (Q : Submonoid (Algebra.GrothendieckGroup P))
      (hQ : FineFan.IsFine Q) (hP : ∀ p : P, Algebra.GrothendieckGroup.of p ∈ Q)
      (S : Submonoid Q),
      ∃ l : logIdealTensorRing A α (integralChartInclusion Q hP) →+*
        logIdealTensorRing A α
          ((integralLocalizationInclusion Q S).comp (integralChartInclusion Q hP)),
        (∀ (a : A) (q : Q),
          l (logIdealTensorBase A α (integralChartInclusion Q hP) a *
            logIdealTensorMonomial A α (integralChartInclusion Q hP) q) =
          logIdealTensorBase A α
            ((integralLocalizationInclusion Q S).comp (integralChartInclusion Q hP)) a *
          logIdealTensorMonomial A α
            ((integralLocalizationInclusion Q S).comp (integralChartInclusion Q hP))
            (integralLocalizationInclusion Q S q)) ∧
        IsOpenImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom l)) ∧
        ∃ E : Localization
            (integralTensorDenominators A α (integralChartInclusion Q hP) S) ≃+*
            logIdealTensorRing A α
              ((integralLocalizationInclusion Q S).comp (integralChartInclusion Q hP)),
          (∀ b : logIdealTensorRing A α (integralChartInclusion Q hP),
            E (algebraMap _ _ b) = l b) ∧
          ∀ (a : A) (q : Q) (s : S),
            E (integralTensorFraction A α (integralChartInclusion Q hP) S a q s) =
              logIdealTensorBase A α
                ((integralLocalizationInclusion Q S).comp (integralChartInclusion Q hP)) a *
              logIdealTensorMonomial A α
                ((integralLocalizationInclusion Q S).comp (integralChartInclusion Q hP))
                (integralMonoidFraction Q S q s)) ∧
    (∀ i : Fin (n + 1), IsIso (pullback.snd
      (integralBaseProjection A α (T.integralSpaceToBase e i))
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (algebraMap A (Localization (MonoidHom.mrange α))))))) ∧
    (∀ z : Localization (MonoidHom.mrange α),
      ∃ (a : A) (s : MonoidHom.mrange α), z = Localization.mk a s) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Monoscheme
